# Path Resolution — 10-src/

This workspace uses Numbered-Functional Architecture with source isolation under `10-src/`.

## Requirements

- All source code path generation, file creation, imports, scripts, and documentation references must point to **`10-src/`**.
- Never use a generic, un-prefixed `src/` folder for new or moved functional resources.
- Un-prefixed `src/` may resolve to stale symlinks or legacy layouts — treat it as forbidden for agent-generated paths.

## Examples

- Correct: `10-src/checkout-skill.py`, `10-src/agents.md`, `10-src/@WHY.md`
- Incorrect: `src/checkout-skill.py`, `./src/agents.md`, `../src/...`

When editing existing packages that legitimately use their own `src/` (e.g. `packages/foo/src/`), that is package-internal layout — not the project functional root. The `10-src/` rule applies to the modular foundational architecture described in `10-src/@WHY.md`.
